  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nThe main forecast challenge will be the development of low stratus\nand areas of freezing fog once again below the inversion, namely\nin the valley regions from Wolf Point to Glasgow. Otherwise, high\npressure looks to maintain dry weather conditions and seasonable\ntemperatures for the next couple of days through Thanksgiving Day.\nIf traveling Thursday, keep in mind the potential for strong and\ngusty west to northwest winds across central and southern Montana,\nwhich could cause dangerous crosswinds.\n\nThese winds will advance into NE Montana For Friday as a front\napproaches. The weekend will feature cooler temperatures and\nperhaps increasing precipitation chances, though the higher\nchances look to remain off to the south and west of the CWA. Those\nwith travel interests for Thanksgiving weekend should keep in mind\nthe rain chances and mountain snows for those portions of the\nstate.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & NBM DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM was largely followed for the forecast period, though the HRRR\nwas blended for visibility and production of fog grids. It showed\nsome utility against recent observations and expected conditions\novernight.",
